{% block body %}
  <main>

    <section class="portfolio-hero" aria-label="CI/CD pipeline">
      <div class="container">
        <a href="../" class="page-back" aria-label="Back to audit cases">← All audit cases</a>
        <p class="eyebrow">CI/CD · Automated deployment</p>
        <h1 class="portfolio-hero__title">
          How to set up a CI/CD pipeline<br>
          to deploy my application<br>
          <em>without stress?</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="portfolio-hero__subtitle">
          A CI/CD pipeline replaces manual deployment with an automated chain:
          lint → tests → deploy. With GitHub Actions, I set up a minimal pipeline
          in 3 to 5 days, no over-engineering, with preview environments
          if your stack supports them.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-group">
          <a href="https://calendly.com/matthieu-viel-fr/30min"
             class="btn btn--primary btn--lg"
             target="_blank"
             rel="noopener noreferrer"
             aria-label="Book a discovery call (opens Calendly)">
            Discuss my project →
          </a>
          <a href="../faq/" class="btn btn--outline btn--lg">
            Frequently asked questions
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cost-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-header">
          <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
          <h2 class="section-title" id="cost-title">What manual deployment really costs</h2>
        </header>
        <div class="prose-wide">
          <p class="prose prose--lead prose--mb-lg">
            Deploying by hand (FTP, SSH, homemade script) creates three constant risks:
            human error, inconsistency between environments,
            and dependency on the person who "knows how it works".
          </p>
          <p class="prose prose--mb-lg">
            Every manual deployment is an anxiety-inducing ceremony.
            There's no safety net: if something breaks in production,
            you find out when a customer tells you.
          </p>
          <p class="prose">
            A CI/CD pipeline isn't a luxury reserved for large teams.
            I set them up for teams of 2 developers.
            The setup time (3 to 5 days) pays for itself with the first
            production bug avoided.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-header section-header--center">
          <p class="eyebrow">The setup</p>
          <h2 class="section-title" id="pipeline-title">A minimal pipeline, in order</h2>
          <p class="section-subtitle">
            Each step has independent value. We add them in order,
            not all at once.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step fade-up">
            <div class="step__number" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
            <h3 class="step__title">Audit current process</h3>
            <p class="step__text">
              How you deploy today, on which hosting provider,
              which environments exist (staging, production).
              This step determines the realistic target.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="step fade-up">
            <div class="step__number" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
            <h3 class="step__title">Lint + automated tests</h3>
            <p class="step__text">
              On every pull request: code verification (ESLint, PHP CS Fixer, Prettier),
              typing (TypeScript), and execution of existing tests.
              Immediate first value.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="step fade-up">
            <div class="step__number" aria-hidden="true">3</div>
            <h3 class="step__title">Automated deployment</h3>
            <p class="step__text">
              On every merge to main: build and automatic deployment
              to staging, then production after validation.
              No more manual deployment.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="avoid-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="layout-2col">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">What we avoid</p>
            <h2 class="section-title section-title--2xl" id="avoid-title">No over-engineering</h2>
            <p class="prose prose--mb">
              For a team of fewer than 5 developers at MVP stage,
              a complex pipeline (matrix builds, canary deployments, feature flags)
              is a distraction, not added value.
            </p>
            <p class="prose prose--mb">
              I set up what you need now, not what you might need in 3 years.
              The pipeline can evolve as the team grows.
            </p>
            <p class="prose">
              GitHub Actions is the pragmatic entry point: free for public repos,
              2,000 minutes/month for private repos on the free plan.
              No additional tool to pay for.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Deliverable</p>
            <h2 class="section-title section-title--2xl">What you receive</h2>
            <ul class="checklist mt-1">
              <li>Operational GitHub Actions pipeline (lint + tests + deploy)</li>
              <li>Pipeline documentation for your team</li>
              <li>Environment variables and secrets configured properly</li>
              <li>Preview environment per pull request (if your stack supports it)</li>
              <li>Team training on pipeline maintenance (2h)</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="solution__note mt-2">
              Timeline: 3 to 5 days depending on your stack complexity and hosting provider.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--alt" aria-label="Related pages">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Go further</p>
        <h2 class="section-title section-title--2xl section-title--mb">Other audit cases</h2>
        <div class="related-audits">
          <a href="../automated-tests-application/">Automated tests</a>
          <a href="../application-vibe-coding-production/">AI-built application</a>
          <a href="../technical-debt-saas-application/">SaaS technical debt</a>
          <a href="../application-solo-founder-clients/">Solo app → first clients</a>
          <a href="../faq/">Technical audit FAQ</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--dark" aria-label="Contact">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="inner-cta">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">First contact</p>
          <h2 class="inner-cta__title">Still on FTP?</h2>
          <p class="inner-cta__text">
            We can automate that. 30 minutes to assess your stack
            and define the right pipeline.
          </p>
          <div class="inner-cta__actions">
            <a href="https://calendly.com/matthieu-viel-fr/30min"
               class="btn btn--outline-light btn--lg"
               target="_blank"
               rel="noopener noreferrer"
               aria-label="Book a discovery call on Calendly (new tab)">
              Book a discovery call →
            </a>
            <a href="mailto:matthieu.viel.fr@gmail.com" class="btn btn--outline-light">
              matthieu.viel.fr@gmail.com
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
{% endblock %}

